<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vladislaus II of Hungary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1456">1456</a>–<a href="/years/1516">1516</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Ladislaus II of Hungary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vladislaus II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagiellonian-dynasty">Jagiellonian dynasty</a>, was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a> in 1471 and King of Hungary in 1490. Weak in both kingdoms, he left power to the estates and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnates</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/land-ordinance-of-vladislaus-ii">Vladislav Land Ordinance</a> of 1500 confirmed noble dominance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>. The double marriage agreement he made with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in 1515 prepared their later succession to both crowns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vladislaus-ii-of-hungary.jpg" alt="Vladislaus II of Hungary" width="320" height="701" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Skot · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vladislaus_II_of_Bohemia_and_Hungary_(1509,_St._Vitus_Cathedral).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
